  "_comment": "The face of every AI without a picture of its own, pinned once (docs/Brand.md, Octo's hatchlings). runtime-contracts (agent_face.rs) checks HATCHLING_FACES and HATCHLING_HASH_MODULUS against hatchlingFaces and hashModulus, parse_hatchling_seed against stamps and notStamps, is_picture_seed against pictures and notPictures, is_octo_handle against octoHandles and notOctoHandles, normalize_face_seed against normalize, fnv1a32_utf16 against hashes (the first three are FNV-1a's published vectors), resolve_agent_face against resolve and default_agent_face against agentDefaults; Studio's copy (packages/frontend/src/utils/aiFace.ts) is tested against the same file. An identity field that is left out is null, and textOnly false. A face is {kind: octo}, {kind: hatchling, n}, {kind: unknown} or {kind: picture, src, fallback}, where fallback is a face that is never a picture. hashed names the normalized string a legacy face was hashed from and its FNV-1a; n is 1 + fnv1a32 mod hashModulus. Strings compare as JavaScript compares them: trimming is String.prototype.trim (it removes U+FEFF and keeps U+0085), lowercasing is toLowerCase (final sigma included), and the hash reads UTF-16 code units.",
